&lt;p&gt;For more information about WorkSource Oregon:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
     &lt;li&gt;Online: &lt;a href="https://www.worksourceoregon.org/"&gt;WorkSourceOregon.org&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
     &lt;li&gt;Phone and address: &lt;a href="https://d1o0i0v5q5lp8h.cloudfront.net/worsou/live/assets/WorkSource%20Oregon%20Office%20Contact%20List.pdf?_t=1714595408"&gt;WorkSource Oregon Center Contact List&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About WorkSource Oregon&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The Oregon Employment Department and the Oregon Department of Human Services are partners in WorkSource Oregon, a consortium of state agencies and local workforce boards, and&amp;nbsp;operates&amp;nbsp;37 WorkSource Oregon centers across the state. WorkSource Oregon offers a wide range of free services&amp;nbsp;to job seekers,&amp;nbsp;employers,&amp;nbsp;and businesses, including&amp;nbsp;personalized career coaching, resume writing, job search strategies,&amp;nbsp;support for job postings&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;hiring incentives, and access to labor-market data. Visit &amp;nbsp;&lt;a href="https://www.worksourceoregon.org/"&gt;worksourceoregon.org&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp; for more information.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

